  "novel_mechanics_found": "L6 expands the cargo mechanic from complementary pairs to two apparent three-part payloads. Rendered colors identify 9+15+14 for the upper-right socket and 6+11+10 for the lower-left socket; solid colors 8, 13, and 12 are decoys, and the orange+magenta dotted socket is impossible because no solid orange cargo exists. Three cargo glyphs visibly fuse and travel together. L6 retains the 60-action hard cutoff and the selection-occlusion mechanic: a green handle can look exposed yet its first destination may still intersect the fused payload and be silently rejected.",
  "narrative": "Fresh-replayed the resolver's 199 labels and confirmed levels_completed=5 before exploration. Across five rendered-frame-only L6 routes, identified the two three-color payloads, fused both, mapped the decoys, and reduced the route to the 60-action cutoff. The best live run placed the 9+15+14 payload deeply into the upper-right dotted socket and the 6+11+10 payload over the lower-left socket, but action 60 still returned GAME_OVER with levels_completed=5; no L6 win was observed. A final fresh reproduce gate replayed the original 199-label prefix and returned reached_level=5, reproduced=true. Step accounting is 199 initial confirmation + 274 exploration/reset calls + 199 gate calls = 672.",
  "gotchas": [
    "L6 has a hard 60-action meter. Action 60 returns GAME_OVER unless the win has already registered; rejected destinations, selection clicks, and no-ops all consume the meter.",
    "The apparent real payloads are 9+15+14 to the upper-right dotted socket and 6+11+10 to the lower-left dotted socket. Solid 8, 13, and 12 are decoys; the orange+magenta dotted glyph is also a decoy/impossible target.",
    "The three-handle carrier should collect 9, then 15, then 14. The two-handle carrier efficiently collects 6, then 11, then 10.",
    "After cargo fusion, a handle center or its intended destination can be occluded even when some green pixels remain visible. A failed selection leaves the previous handle selected, while a blocked move is a silent no-op; always verify the blue-line endpoint before batching more clicks.",
    "Move the currently selected exposed handle far enough to shift the fused payload away before selecting a buried handle. In the upper route, moving the 42,19 handle toward 50,13 exposes the other endpoints.",
    "Handle moves remain radius-8 Euclidean teleports. Diagonals such as (3,7), (4,6), and (5,6) are legal; (4,7), (6,6), and (7,4) are silently rejected.",
    "A normal RESET action restarts L6 without replaying levels 1-5, but the final replay artifact intentionally remains the original 199-label verified prefix because no L6 win was observed."
  ],
